                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Tri-Motors Safety Airways/47:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-19T10:00:00-03:30">June 19, 1929—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>30. Department’s telegram 8, April 30, 2 p.m.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d476-f1"/>
                    Permission for free entry and flights granted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
